    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** serving as our primary offensive engine, boasting a strong 73.88 efficiency score. Despite the potential for a lower stolen base floor against a pitcher with an elite hold rate, **Corbin Carroll** remains our most critical asset against Junis, as his position in the #2 hole and a favorable platoon matchup mitigate the risk. **Josh Naylor** also anchors the lineup with a 65.49 score; while he faces the respectable P. Lambert, his position in the heart of the order and a +5% boost from dynamic platoon modeling solidify him as an essential start. Conversely, **Gabriel Moreno** and **Cole Young** are relegated to the bottom of the order, suppressing their scores to 53.89 and 40.36 respectively, keeping them in \"marginal\" territory where they must capitalize on early-game efficiency to avoid being pulled late.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s card was the exclusion of **Travis Bazzana**, who narrowly missed the starting threshold with a 38.06 score. While his underlying xwOBA of 0.394 is promising, the rigorous efficiency standard required to burn game caps left him on the pine, as the L/L platoon disadvantage against Suter created too much volatility for his current profile. Meanwhile, **Jose Caballero** remains on our bench, not due to lack of production, but due to his exclusion from the official starting lineup, rendering him a zero for the day\u2019s rotation. With **James Wood** and **Mickey Moniak** also sidelined by team off-days, our offensive depth is heavily consolidated into the four starters. We will monitor the lineup health for **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Austin Riley**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, **Carson Williams**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Kyle Karros**, **Luis Campusano**, and **Alex Freeland** as we navigate this stretch of the 2026 campaign, ensuring that no game caps are wasted on sub-optimal plate appearances.",
